IBMRA1.SYS ("IBM Rapid Access Keyboard I enabler")

The original driver was released in 2001 by Bart van Leeuwen. Its readme
(doc\original\readme.txt) contains only:

    v0.0.1 (C) 2001 Bart van Leeuwen <bart@netage.nl>
    ...
    Disclaimer:
    Use this software at you own risk.
    Its stil a Alpha version !

No license text, no permission to copy, modify or redistribute, and no
statement placing the code in the public domain was found in the original
source, in the original readme, or in the repository history.

The driver is based on OS/2 physical device driver sample code by Rick Fishman
(Code Blazers, Inc.) published in the Fall 1991 issue of IBM Personal Systems
Developer and adapted for Watcom C/C++ by WATCOM International Corp. That code
also carries no license text in this repository.

Therefore the rights to this code are NOT clear. No permission is granted to
use, copy, modify or redistribute the driver or its source code. Do not publish
or distribute it until the rights holder(s) have clarified the license.

The files added in 2026 (src\version.h, src\include\I8042.H, src\bldlevel.lnk,
sample\ibmra1.c, test\, the build scripts and the documentation) are offered
under the same terms as the rest of the project and do not grant any rights
beyond those that the original authors grant.

See README.md ("License") and doc\PROVENANCE.md for the origin of the files and
the comparison with the IBM DDK.
